## DEFINITION
I-TASSER (Iterative Threading ASSEmbly Refinement) is an online tool used to predict the three-dimensional (3D) structure and function
of proteins from their amino acid sequences.

## PURPOSE
- Predict 3D protein structures.
- Predict protein function.
- Identify structural templates.
- Support protein modeling studies.

## FEATURES
- Protein structure prediction.
- Function and ligand-binding site prediction.
- Template-based modeling.
- Structure refinement and confidence estimation.

## IMPORTANT SCORES
- **C-score:** Confidence of the predicted model (higher is better).
- **TM-score:** Measures structural similarity (values >0.5 generally indicate a correct fold).
- **RMSD:** Estimates structural deviation from the native structure (lower is better).

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- Protein FASTA (.fasta, .fa)
- Protein sequence (.txt)

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Accepts amino acid sequences only.
- Generates multiple predicted 3D models.
- Provides confidence scores for model evaluation.
- Widely used for protein structure and function prediction.
